1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,300
Sometimes there are no labels. Clustering finds natural groups, like customers who shop the same way.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:18,500
Place k centres, give each point to its nearest centre, move each centre to the middle of its points, and repeat until nothing moves.

3
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:26,050
How many groups? Try several values of k, and watch how tight the groups are.

4
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:31,900
When adding another group stops helping much, you have found the elbow.

5
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:37,575
Scale the features first, or the biggest numbers decide the groups.

6
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:47,730
A shop might find bargain hunters, weekend families and big monthly buyers, and market to each one differently.

7
00:00:48,430 --> 00:00:54,955
Clusters are suggestions. Give each one a name only after looking at who is inside.

